&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;As our Expert, Treasury ALM, you will run the day-to-day engine of a multi-entity treasury function spanning traditional finance and digital assets. Reporting to the Manager of Treasury, you will manage liquidity and balance sheet operations across a multi-regulatory structure handling 12+ fiat currencies and 700+ digital assets. You will serve as a key subject matter expert bridging the gap between traditional banking frameworks and 24/7 crypto liquidity.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ALM &amp;amp; Risk Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage duration and liquidity mismatches across traditional and crypto markets, monitoring the IRRBB framework and stress-testing the balance sheet against aggressive market pivots.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Digital Asset Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Monitor live crypto risk incidents under pressure, measuring real-time exposures and instructing prompt corrective measures on long and short positions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Risk Contribution &amp;amp; Regulatory Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Deliver strategic proposals to the Financial Risk Forum covering long-term investments, ALM netting arrangements, and MMF allocations, while contributing directly to prudential requirements delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Ownership &amp;amp; Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive treasury framework optimizations, refine analytical models, and act as an individual contributor subject matter expert in close collaboration with key internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Integrity &amp;amp; Reconciliation:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the quality of the data feeding treasury and ALM reporting, ensuring figures reconcile cleanly across source systems, and diagnosing and remediating weak or semi-manual data ingestion processes so that reporting is timely, accurate and audit-ready&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3+ Years of Core Treasury Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; You bring at least 3 years of hands-on experience in corporate treasury or financial institutions, specifically managing complex asset-liability management (ALM) structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dual-Asset Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Deeply comfortable operating simultaneously in traditional finance (SWIFT, SEPA, physical/notional pooling) and digital asset markets (handling stablecoins and a broad spectrum of crypto assets).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Mastery:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong working knowledge of multi-entity regulatory frameworks, specifically MiCAR, EMI, and MiFID II, with direct experience handling capital compliance and risk appetite frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data &amp;amp; System Savvy:&lt;/strong&gt; Experienced in leveraging Treasury Management Systems (TMS), banking APIs, and blockchain analytics to maintain early-warning indicators like Hedging Efficiency Dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluent in English:&lt;/strong&gt; Professional working proficiency in written and spoken English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
