&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining our Group Reporting team, you will contribute to group consolidation activities and handle day-to-day IFRS accounting topics. You will manage core Intercompany reconciliations to resolve discrepancies and support timely, accurate financial closes. As an active team contributor assisting with year-end audits and financial statement disclosures, you will help maintain high reporting standards and streamline our finance operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform hands-on month-end, quarter-end, and year-end closing tasks within the group consolidation workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in drafting IFRS annual financial statements, disclosures, and supporting technical notes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute Intercompany (IC) reconciliations to ensure accurate eliminations across entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the team during year-end external audits by preparing supporting schedules, documentation, and answering routine queries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify practical ways to improve consolidation templates and daily financial reporting workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of hands-on experience in group accounting, consolidation, or audit support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good practical understanding of IFRS standards and experience assisting with financial statement notes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on exposure to year-end audit preparation and compiling clean audit working papers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working familiarity with group reporting software or standard ERP systems (experience with LucaNet is a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliable team player who works comfortably in fast-paced fintech environments and meets tight reporting schedules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
